1. Download and extract the project

Download the latest project ZIP

Extract it somewhere simple, for example:

C:\Projects\NestWise-Pakistan
2. Make sure these are installed

You need:

Node.js — preferably Node 20+
Python — preferably Python 3.11+
Git — mainly for GitHub/CI/CD
Docker Desktop — optional, only if you want to run it through Docker

Check them in PowerShell:

node --version
npm --version
python --version
git --version
3. Run the Flask backend

Open the extracted project folder.

Then open PowerShell/Terminal inside the project and go to the backend folder. Depending on where you extracted it:

cd C:\Projects\NestWise-Pakistan

If the project has a backend folder:

cd backend

Create a Python virtual environment:

python -m venv venv

Activate it:

.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

If PowerShell gives an execution-policy error, run:

Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass

Then activate again:

.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1

Install backend packages:

pip install -r requirements.txt

Then start Flask:

python app.py

You should see something similar to:

Running on http://127.0.0.1:5000

Keep this terminal open.

4. Run the React.js frontend

Open a second PowerShell window.

Go to the project frontend folder:

cd C:\Projects\NestWise-Pakistan\frontend

Install React dependencies:

npm install

Then start React:

npm run dev

You should get something similar to:

Local: http://localhost:5173/

Open:

http://localhost:5173

in Chrome.

Your structure should basically work like:

Browser
   ↓
React.js
localhost:5173
   ↓ REST API
Python Flask
localhost:5000
   ↓
SQLite Database
