6. Run with Docker instead

Because I also added Docker support, you can use Docker Desktop instead of manually starting React and Flask.

Open Docker Desktop first.

Then from the main project directory run:

docker compose up --build

The first build can install all the required dependencies.

To stop it:

docker compose down
7. How the CI/CD pipeline runs

You do not manually run the GitHub Actions pipeline in the normal workflow.

Upload/push the project to GitHub:

git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial NestWise full stack project"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin YOUR_GITHUB_REPOSITORY_URL
git push -u origin main

Then go to:

GitHub Repository
→ Actions

You should see the NestWise pipeline.

On a push to main, GitHub Actions will handle the pipeline stages such as:

Push Code
   ↓
Backend CI
   ↓
Frontend CI
   ↓
React Production Build
   ↓
Docker Validation
   ↓
Docker Build
   ↓
CD / Deployment Artifact
If you only want to run the project normally

You only need two terminals:

Terminal 1

cd backend
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python app.py

Terminal 2

cd frontend
npm run dev

Then visit:

http://localhost:5173
